import json
from pathlib import Path
from assembly_record_writer import write_record
p=Path(__file__).with_name('assembly_wardlow.json')
d=json.loads(p.read_text())
d['kernel']=d['kernel'].replace('Earlier actual Records must be screened at release; the January 12 group shares its entering baseline, and alphabetical assignment order makes no same-day law dependency.', 'The other effective earlier Records—Lesage, Fiore, Drye, Torres, Steamfitters and Kimel—change no stop or suppression premise. Paul, United Reporting and Hill have no effective event or count. Laidlaw, written earlier on January 12 for alphabetical assignment order, is counted but supplies no entering substantive authority for this uncoordinated same-day case. The January 12 group retains its common entering-law baseline, including the group continuing in the next chunk.')
d['blocks']['Opinion Topology']="| Writing | Author | Joined by | Relationship to judgment | Scope joined |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Opinion of the Court | {AUTHOR} | {FULL_JOINERS} in full; O'Connor, Scalia, Kennedy and Thomas as to Part I only | Five-Justice affirmance | All nine join the governing rule in Part I; five join application and remedy in Part II |\n| Dissent in part | O'Connor | Scalia, Kennedy, Thomas | Would reverse the initial-stop ruling and remand | Disagrees with Part II; joins Part I's common rule |"
d['blocks']['Separate Writings']="Justice O'Connor, joined by Scalia, Kennedy and Thomas, agrees with the governing totality rule but finds reasonable suspicion here. Wardlow looked toward the officers and immediately ran through a gangway and alley in the credited narcotics setting. For the dissent, that temporal sequence and evasive route provide the individualized conduct missing from a location-only stop. Police recognition can reasonably be inferred without proving that he noticed every vehicle, and an innocent explanation need not defeat every grounded investigative inference. The dissent assumes neither marked cars nor an actual crowd, transaction, pre-stop firearm or guilty motive; the trial court's racial observation supplies no suspicion. It applies Ornelas's controlling independent review while giving weight to supported local inferences; Scalia retains his prior objection to that review allocation. The four would reverse the initial-stop ruling and remand for any properly remaining issue, without automatically reinstating the conviction or deciding the separate frisk and bag search."
d['continuity'] += " O'Connor authors the published application dissent, joined by Scalia, Kennedy and Thomas. Their sufficient-inference position does not change the all-nine common rule; Scalia's prior review-allocation objection remains noncontrolling."
p.write_text(json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
write_record(p,'Stone-Zsela',d['lead_support'],"Stone self-assigns this bounded application. The required legal work is to credit the actual narcotics setting and allow the recognition inference, yet explain the insufficient individualized connection without turning the result into a flight exclusion or a mandatory third-factor rule. His approved formulation expressly supplies that precise combination and reservation, which every necessary joiner supports. Stevens is the strongest alternative: his Dickerson and Ornelas positions support the same grounded review, and he also has zero counted leads. Stone's concrete advantage is fidelity to the already supported formulation separating this record's inference from a new reusable police-stop rule, not his office, agreement with the result or case importance. Breyer likewise has zero; no lower-count preference favors another pool member. No new accommodation or changed vote is claimed.",True)
